{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975)."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"fileName":"AhoCorasickAutomaton.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton.swift#L29"},"modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","externalID":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/Match","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/MatchesView","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/init(patterns:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternCount","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/stateCount","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/containsMatch(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/firstMatch(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/matches(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternLength(at:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternLength(checkedAt:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is the trie of the patterns with two more links per state: the failure link, to the state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the longest proper suffix of the state’s prefix that is also a prefix of some pattern, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the output link, to the nearest state along the failure links at which a pattern ends. A scan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"follows the trie while the text matches and the failure links where it stops matching, so it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads each symbol of the text once and reports all the matches in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for a text of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols with "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}]},{"type":"text","text":" matches."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","for match in automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\") {","    print(match.patternIndex, match.range)","}","\/\/ 1 1..<4   (\"she\")","\/\/ 0 2..<4   (\"he\")","\/\/ 3 2..<6   (\"hers\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matches come in order of where they end, and of those ending at one place, longest first."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Ranges count the text’s symbols from 0. The automaton is built once and is immutable."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Symbols are mapped to dense indices at construction, through a 256-entry table when they are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt8"},{"type":"text","text":" and a dictionary otherwise, so a scan over bytes, such as a string’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"utf8"},{"type":"text","text":", does no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hashing. When the states times the distinct symbols are few enough, every transition is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"precomputed into a table, and a scan takes one load per symbol."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries":{"title":"Tries","abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tri